ror":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The coupon discount was being applied twice. I fixed it, and all 9 tests pass, including a new one for coupon orders.\n\n**The bug** was in `src/cart.js:24`, inside `calcTotal`:\n\n```js\nconst discount = subtotal - applyCoupon(subtotal, cart.coupon)\nconst taxable = applyCoupon(subtotal - discount, cart.coupon)  // coupon applied again\n```\n\n`subtotal - discount` is already the discounted amount, but it went through `applyCoupon` a second time. With a 10% coupon on a 3000 order, customers paid tax on 2430 (two 10% cuts) instead of 2700. The total came out as 2673 when it should have been 2970. The returned `discount` still showed only one discount, so the breakdown didn't add up to the total either.\n\n**The fix** removes the second call:\n\n```js\nconst taxable = subtotal - discount\n```\n\n**The test:** I added one in `test/cart.test.js` for a `WELCOME10` order, since no existing test covered a coupon at checkout. It checks for subtotal 3000, discount 300, tax 270 and total 2970.","ttft_ms":1676,"type":"result","duration_ms":17125,"uuid":"07609586-8f62-41d9-a239-4b415018f999","ttft_stream_ms":1230,"time_to_request_ms":265,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":64,"system_prompt":99,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":3,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":20,"engine_pickup":14,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":4,"autocompact":3,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":12,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":2,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":36,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":390,"time_to_request_major_faults":8953,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"environment","slowest_producer_ms":13,"cpu_ms":15,"major_faults":426},"first_content_frame_ms":1231,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
